-- title:
--   Uniqueness: every admissible $\Phi$ gives $\mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]=\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}[g(X_{t_n})\mid\mathcal F_{t_i}]$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $X$ is the recombining binomial tree of (3.11): nodes $x_{i,0}<\dots<x_{i,i}$ at time $t_i$ ($0\le i\le N$), up-probabilities $0<p^+_{i,j}<1$; $\varphi_{t_1},\dots,\varphi_{t_N}$ are distortion functions and $\varphi_{t_0}(p)=p$; $G_{i,j}=\mathbb P(X_{t_i}\ge x_{i,j})$, $G_{i,i+1}=0$; $q^\pm_{i,j}$ and $\mathbb Q$ are given by (3.13) and (3.15); and condition (3.14) holds.
--
--   Let $\Psi$ be a time-consistent dynamic distortion function with the initial condition $\Psi(t_0,t_n,x_{0,0};p)=\varphi_{t_n}(p)$ for $n=1,\dots,N$ and $p\in[0,1]$, and let $\mathcal E_{s,t}$ be its conditional nonlinear expectation (2.11). Then
--   $$
--   \mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]=\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}\bigl[g(X_{t_n})\mid\mathcal F_{t_i}\bigr]\qquad\text{for all }0\le i<n\le N,\ g\in\mathcal I .
--   $$
--
--   So the conditional nonlinear expectation of any admissible $\Psi$ is determined: it is the $\mathbb Q$-conditional expectation.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a Markov process X on an abstract filtered probability space with transition law (3.11) and the filtration F = F^X it generates → the canonical path space Fin N → Bool (true = up) with path weights ∏ p^±, and X_{t_i}(ω) = x_{i, number of up-moves before i}; reason: every quantity in the statement depends only on the law of X and on F^X; the same instances
--   - encoding: times 0 = t_0 < ⋯ < t_N → time indices 0, …, N (Φ(t_i, t_n, x; p) is Φ i n x p, φ_{t_n} is φ n); reason: the times enter only as labels
--   - encoding: the assumption φ_0(p) := p → phiExt φ 0 = id built into the definitions; the value φ 0 of the given family is ignored; reason: the same convention, without a hypothesis on φ 0
--   - encoding: conditioning on F_{t_i} (resp. σ(X_{t_i})) and identities between random variables → conditioning on the atom of F_{t_i} containing ω (resp. on the event {X_{t_i} = X_{t_i}(ω)}), identities stated at every path ω; reason: F_{t_i} = σ(X_{t_0}, …, X_{t_i}) is generated by these atoms, and every path has positive probability, so almost-sure identities are identities at every path
--   - encoding: ∫₀^∞ Φ(s, t, X_s; ℙ(ξ ≥ x | F_s)) dx → Bochner integral over (0, ∞) of the same integrand; reason: the integrand is bounded with bounded support for every ξ the statement uses, so the integral is finite and equals the paper's
--   - encoding: Φ jointly Lebesgue measurable in (x, p) → NullMeasurable for the Lebesgue measure of ℝ × [0, 1] (volume on ℝ × ℝ restricted to univ ×ˢ Icc 0 1); reason: null-measurability for Lebesgue measure is Lebesgue measurability
--   - reading: "Assume Φ is an arbitrary time-consistent dynamic distortion function" → Ψ is a time-consistent dynamic distortion function with the initial condition Ψ(t_0, t_n, x_{0,0}; ·) = φ_{t_n} on [0, 1], n = 1, …, N; reason: the uniqueness part of Theorem 3.4 is among functions with the initial condition, and the proof uses it (first display, p.15)
-- source:
--   Ma–Wong–Zhang, Time-consistent conditional expectation under probability distortion, arXiv:1809.08262v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4, last paragraph, p.15

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Distortion
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Tree
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Dynamic

open MeasureTheory Set

namespace DistortedCondExp

/-- **Every admissible `Φ` gives the `ℚ`-conditional expectation** (Ma–Wong–Zhang,
arXiv:1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4, p.15: "This implies further that
`𝓔_{t_i,t_{i+1}}[g(X_{t_{i+1}})] = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_{i+1}}) | F_{t_i}]`. Now both `𝓔_{t_i,t_n}` and `𝔼^ℚ[·|·]`
satisfy the tower property, then `𝓔_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})] = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | F_{t_i}]` for all
`t_i < t_n` and all `g ∈ ℐ`."). Under (3.14), if `Ψ` is a time-consistent dynamic distortion
function with the initial condition `Ψ(t_0, t_n, x_{0,0}; ·) = φ_{t_n}` for `n = 1, …, N`, then
`𝓔^Ψ_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})] = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | F_{t_i}]` for all `0 ≤ i < n ≤ N` and `g ∈ ℐ`.

**Formalization Note** `𝔼^ℚ[· | F_{t_i}]` at the path `ω` is the `ℚ`-conditional expectation given
the atom `histAtom i ω` of `F_{t_i}`; the identity is stated at every path. -/
theorem uniqueness_condE (N : ℕ) (x p : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (φ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (htree : IsBinomialTree N x p) (hφ : ∀ n, 1 ≤ n → n ≤ N → IsDistortion (φ n))
    (h314 : Cond314 N x p φ)
    (Ψ : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (hΨ : IsDynamicDistortion N Ψ) (hTC : IsTimeConsistent N x p Ψ)
    (hinit : InitialCondition N x φ Ψ) :
    ∀ i n, i < n → n ≤ N → ∀ g : ℝ → ℝ, InI g → ∀ ω : Path N,
      condE x p Ψ i n (fun ω' => g (X x n ω')) ω =
        cexp (qPlus N x p φ) (fun ω' => g (X x n ω')) (histAtom i ω) := by sorry

end DistortedCondExp
